# Vendored third-party payloads are byte-pinned: each package's VERSION file
# records a SHA-256 per file, and tests/test_local_first_assets.py checks it.
#
# This repository is `core.autocrlf=true` with no root .gitattributes, so a text
# payload committed as LF materializes as CRLF in a Windows checkout and LF in a
# Linux one. That is the same commit with two different digests, and it would
# red the digest contract on whichever platform it was not pinned from. It would
# also quietly falsify the packet's central claim — that the bytes we serve are
# the bytes upstream published.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the packages this rule was written for. `fontawesome/`,
# `free-exercise-db/` and `musclemap/` predate it and are left alone on purpose:
# switching an already-checked-out tree to `-text` makes git report every one of
# their text files as modified, which is a separate change with its own review.
bootstrap/** -text
flatpickr/** -text
inter/** -text
popperjs/** -text
sortable/** -text
tippy/** -text
